50-set-functions: set functions applied from Python.

Seam: set0, set1 and set2 of Control.SetFunctions applied to symbols of a
module and to Python values; sortValues, isEmpty and values2list (an IO
goal) read the set back; a free variable from curry.free() as the argument.
Sources: memo A1 (the call form), section 4 item 13; catalogue P24 (the
tail); issue #117 (closed; regression); decisions D25 to D28; issues #133
and #134 (open, related, not pinned).
Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: none; PAKCS 3.4.1 under --nocypm cannot load a
module that imports Control.SetFunctions.

Expected output: set0 coin is [0, 1]; set2 rule gives the one command;
a function that fails gives the empty set and isEmpty True; set1 inc coin
gives two sets, one per value of the argument, which the set function does
not encapsulate; ord2 gives ([10], 0) and ([11], 1) (#117: the captured
choice is made outside the set); twice is [0, 1, 1, 2]; a failing argument
gives no value, for sortValues and for isEmpty alike (the deferred rule);
nested is [[0, 1]]; the free argument gives 11 values, 9 empty sets and
the sets ["cmd1"] and ["cmd2"]; values2list yields its payload.
